From: juansolo457 <5344231+Juansolo457@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:27:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] Settings menu: controller navigation through slider rows

On the classic settings pages the D-pad and stick stopped at the first slider:
focus moved into the slider's number box, which takes every arrow key. Up and
down on a slider also stepped its value on the way past.

- A slider's paired number box and list scrollbars are no longer focus stops; a
  box focused by the mouse hands focus to its slider on the next D-pad press.
- A direction reaches the focused control only if that control uses it
  (choices and horizontal sliders: left/right; vertical sliders and lists:
  up/down; edit boxes: left/right, plus up/down when the text wraps). Every
  other direction moves focus.
- A works like a click: on a choice it steps to the next value.
- Controller focus runs the row's "<row>_hover" scripts, so the row lights up
  (and plays its hover sound) as it does under the mouse.
- A focused row outside a scrolled list's view asks the menu to scroll it in
  (scrollIntoView); the menu scrolls the least that shows the whole row.

menu_controller_navigation.py covers the traversal, direction ownership, row
highlight and the scroll math.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
